.TH tupng n 0.4 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tupng
.PP
A pure\-Tcl PNG \fBencoder/decoder\fR \-\- no Tk, no external packages, only the core \fBzlib\fR command. It complements \fBtclutils::tuimage\fR (which inspects PNG headers). The encoder writes 8\-bit images in four colour types:
.TS
l l l.
Function	Colour type	Pixel syntax
\fBencodeRGB\fR / \fBwriteRGB\fR	truecolour (2)	\fBRRGGBB\fR / \fB#rrggbb\fR / \fB{r g b}\fR
\fBencodeRGBA\fR / \fBwriteRGBA\fR	truecolour+alpha (6)	\fBRRGGBBAA\fR / \fB{r g b a}\fR
\fBencodeGray\fR / \fBwriteGray\fR	grayscale (0)	integer 0..255
\fBencodeIndexed\fR / \fBwriteIndexed\fR	palette (3)	integer index into palette
.TE
.PP
The image model is a list of rows; each row is a list of pixels and all rows must have equal length. \fBencode*\fR return PNG bytes; \fBwrite*\fR write them to a file. Two raw helpers, \fBencodeRGBARaw\fR / \fBwriteRGBARaw\fR, take pre\-packed \fBwidth*height*4\fR RGBA bytes directly (the encode side of \fBdecode\fR).
.CS
set png [tupng::encodeRGB {{FF0000 00FF00} {0000FF FFFFFF}}]
tupng::writeRGBA out.png {{FF0000FF 00FF0080} {0000FF00 FFFFFFFF}} -compression 9
tupng::writeIndexed out.png {FF0000 0000FF00} {{0 1} {1 0}}   ;# entry 1 transparent
.CE
.SS Options
.IP \(bu
\fB\-compression 0..9\fR (default 6) \-\- zlib level.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-filter best|none|sub|up|average|paeth\fR (default \fBbest\fR). \fBbest\fR picks a per\-scanline filter using the minimum\-sum\-of\-absolute\-differences heuristic (fast); the fixed modes force one filter.
.SS "Notes / limits"
.PP
8\-bit depth only; no 16\-bit and no interlacing. For indexed images the palette holds 1..256 entries; a palette entry with alpha < 255 emits a \fBtRNS\fR chunk. Truecolour alpha (RGBA) is stored inline (type 6). Reuses only \fBtclutils::common\fR (option parsing) and the core \fBzlib\fR.
.SS "Decoding (0.3)"
.PP
\fBtupng::decode bytes\fR and \fBtupng::readPNG file\fR reconstruct an 8\-bit, non\-interlaced PNG (colour types 0/2/3/4/6) and return a dict: \fBwidth height colortype bitdepth rgba\fR, where \fBrgba\fR is width\fIheight\fR4 packed bytes (row\-major R G B A) \-\- the inverse of \fBencodeRGBARaw\fR, so encode/decode round\-trips byte\-exactly. Errors carry \fB{TCLUTILS TUPNG DECODE <reason>}\fR (SIGNATURE, IHDR, BITDEPTH, INTERLACE, COLORTYPE, IDAT, FILTER). 16\-bit and interlaced PNGs are not supported.
